@clawsweeper re-review

The merge conflict is resolved at b9f4639c377a323f5efc37a9ac44321f986cd789. The PR body now records macOS final-effect proof at the exact native/reset boundary raised in the previous review: unchanged production Swift code, the actual `removeStateAndLinkedPaths` operation, and a writer paused after admission immediately before `sqlite3_step`. DELETE-mode reset completed and the resumed write returned `SQLITE_READONLY_DBMOVED` (1032), preserving both the retired inode and a replacement database. WAL/active-transaction reset refused with state intact. The same paused writer without reset committed successfully.

The WAL integration passed independent P0/P1 review, production and affected test types, targeted lint, and 47 runtime tests. Application schema remains version 18 from main; no table change is introduced relative to main. Exact-head Linux Package Acceptance from published `openclaw@2026.9.4` is running at https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/36066342907 and is still required before landing.
